# repos — the Fossify upstreams this docs-only carrier pins and documents.
#
# One line per upstream:  <repo_url> <pin_sha>   # <tag> <date>
#
# fetch.sh clones each into checkout/<name>/ (name = the repo's basename) and
# detaches it at its pin; apply.sh applies that repo's comment-only streams
# (patches/<name>/docs then book). Blank lines and #-comments are ignored;
# only the first two whitespace fields (URL, SHA) are read.
#
# Each pin is a RELEASED TAG's commit (conservative, stable anchors), not a
# moving branch tip — the reference set's file:line anchors and the book's
# doc-region spans must not rot under us. Fossify apps are mid-migration from
# classic Views/XML to Jetpack Compose, so a fixed tag also freezes which UI
# stack the documented code uses (record it per doc; see CLAUDE.md).
#
# Commons is the documentation centre of gravity — every app depends on it, so
# it is documented in depth; the four apps below are thin exemplars (Gallery's
# media pipeline, Phone's telephony/SIM, Messages' SMS/MMS, Keyboard's IME).

